From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: recreate the OLE clipboard window when its thread has ended

Purpose: copying files in XP Explorer keeps working after a folder window
has been closed.
Windows behavior: the OLE clipboard works from any thread that has
initialized OLE, whatever happened to the threads that used it before.
Wine before: the process has one hidden clipboard window, made by the first
thread that needs it. Windows are destroyed with their thread, but the
handle was kept, so every later OleSetClipboard in the process failed in
OpenClipboard with CLIPBRD_E_CANT_OPEN. XP Explorer calls OleFlushClipboard
when a folder window closes, which makes the window even if nothing was ever
copied, and then the window's thread ends: from then on Copy in the shell
process did nothing and Paste stayed grey.
Change: get_clipbrd_window() makes a new window when the old handle is no
longer a window.
Evidence: tests/ole-clipboard-thread.c (0x800401d0 before, S_OK after); on
the EeePC the Windows clipboard's sequence number was still 1 after copies in
the shell process, while a new Explorer process copied.
Scope: all programs; only a destroyed clipboard window is replaced.
---
 dlls/ole32/clipboard.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
diff --git a/dlls/ole32/clipboard.c b/dlls/ole32/clipboard.c
index c546089..88d1d1b 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/clipboard.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/clipboard.c
@@ -1899,7 +1899,9 @@ static HWND create_clipbrd_window(void);
  */
 static inline HRESULT get_clipbrd_window(ole_clipbrd *clipbrd, HWND *wnd)
 {
-    if ( !clipbrd->window )
+    /* The window belongs to the thread that made it and is destroyed when that
+     * thread ends, while the process and its OLE clipboard go on. */
+    if ( !clipbrd->window || !IsWindow(clipbrd->window) )
         clipbrd->window = create_clipbrd_window();
 
     *wnd = clipbrd->window;
